      "writtenOn": "2021-08-24T16:47:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is confusing. I think we should remove #ifdef CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC_LOW_POWER from struct tcpm_drv definition (and define enter_low_power_mode to NULL):\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC_LOW_POWER\n\t/**\n\t * Instructs the TCPC to enter into low power mode.\n\t *\n\t * NOTE: Do no use tcpc_(read|write) style helper methods in this\n\t * function. You must use i2c_(read|write) directly.\n\t *\n\t * @param port Type-C port number\n\t *\n\t * @return EC_SUCCESS or error\n\t */\n\tint (*enter_low_power_mode)(int port);\n#endif\n\nThis will allow a hybrid combination (one with LPM and another without LPM).\n\nWe probably don\u0027t need CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC_LOW_POWER at all since we can do the same check by enter_low_power_mode \u003d\u003d NULL.",
